@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-wire-service
`proto/dfs.proto` MUST expose the unary `Dfs` service specified here. Create, update, write, rename,
and remove MUST be variants of `Apply.operations`, not separate RPCs or streaming mutation groups.
Lists and maps MAY be empty unless a minimum is specified. Sizes and offsets MUST be byte counts.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;api] dfs-bearer-authority
Calls MUST authenticate through `authorization: Bearer <key>` gRPC metadata. Keys MUST be opaque
64-character bearer strings. `CreateTenant` MUST require the server key. `CreateSession`,
`ListGrants`, and `UpdateGrants` MUST require a tenant key and derive the tenant exclusively from
that authenticated key; their requests MUST NOT contain a tenant ID. All other RPCs MUST require
an active session key and derive the tenant and subjects exclusively from it.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] dfs-grant-authorization
Filesystem and search access MUST use the effective grant permissions for the session's subjects.
The server MUST enforce these permissions on every call; mount/client checks of `Attr.mode` MUST NOT
replace server authorization. Ordinary reads MUST conceal inaccessible objects as `NOT_FOUND`;
`Validate` MAY report `DENIED` explicitly. Mutation permission failures MUST use `FORBIDDEN`.
Tenant-key administration MUST NOT be restricted by object grants.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-grant-shape
Each `Grant` MUST select exactly one ALLOW or DENY variant. ALLOW MUST contain a nonempty subject
and a mode; DENY MUST contain only a mode and apply to every session. JSON DENY payloads MUST reject
a subject rather than silently interpret the rule as applying to everyone. Subjects MUST be matched
exactly and case-sensitively against the tenant-key holder's asserted session subjects. The server
MUST NOT resolve group membership or infer additional subjects from strings such as
`u:spolu@dust.tt` or `g:engineering`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] dfs-grant-inheritance
Effective permissions MUST start at zero and be evaluated along the real ancestor chain from tenant
root through the target. At each object, all local DENY modes MUST first remove inherited
permissions, then matching local ALLOW modes MUST be ORed in:
`(inherited & (~denies & 0o7)) | allows`. Matching ALLOW MUST win over DENY at the same object
regardless of attachment order. An ALLOW at the same object or deeper MUST be able to restore denied
permissions; evaluation MUST continue through zero inherited permissions. Direct IDs and `/shared`
aliases MUST use the same full ancestor chain, including hidden ancestors.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;api] dfs-read-permissions
`Stat`, `Read`, and `ReadFiles` MUST require r on each real target. `Lookup` MUST require x on a
real parent and r on its returned child. `List` MUST require rx on a real directory and return only
children with r. `Search` MUST require r on each hit and rx on a supplied scope directory.
`Validate` MUST require r on each real target and additionally x for a directory content-version
check. Virtual root/shared MUST support namespace reads as read-only projections, checking real
entries separately. The x bit MUST control directory traversal; the API MUST NOT expose a
file-execution RPC.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;api] dfs-mutation-permissions
Create MUST require wx on its parent. Update and write MUST require w on their target. Rename MUST
require w on the source and any replacement and wx on affected parents. Remove MUST require w on its
target and wx on its parent. Each participating object's mode MUST be evaluated independently
against its real ancestor chain. Read validation MUST NOT authorize cached mutations; every mutation
MUST independently check its required permissions.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-grant-identity
Grant identity MUST include the variant, subject for ALLOW, and mode. Identical values MUST
deduplicate; distinct modes for one subject and distinct DENY modes MUST remain separate attachments
whose modes combine during evaluation. Changing a mode MUST detach the old value and attach the new
one. Attaching an existing value or detaching an absent value MUST be a no-op.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;backend] dfs-authorization-freshness
Authorization MAY use a complete permission tree within its freshness bound, 30 seconds by default.
Expired or unusable tree proofs MUST fall back to current FDB authorization. File metadata and
content reads MUST use FDB; asynchronous search indexing has an independent lag.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-identifiers
`ObjectId.value` MUST contain exactly 16 UUIDv7 bytes and identify a real stored object, including
the tenant root. Identity MUST remain stable across renames and moves. `ObjectRef` MUST select
exactly one real ID or virtual `root`/`shared` tag; a selected boolean tag MUST be true. Virtual
root MUST remain distinct from the stored tenant root. Only `Stat`, `Lookup`, `List`, and `Validate`
MUST accept virtual references as targets; other operations MUST require real IDs.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-timestamps
`Attr.atime/mtime/ctime`, `ExtendedMetadata.created`, `Session.expires_at`,
`UpdateOperation.atime/mtime`, and `SearchFilter.modified_after/modified_before` MUST use unsigned
Unix milliseconds, with one-millisecond precision and no dates before the epoch. Zero MUST mean the
epoch; omission of an optional timestamp MUST remain distinct from zero.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-input-limits
Tenant IDs MUST contain 1–256 UTF-8 bytes; subjects MUST contain 1–1,024 UTF-8 bytes. Basenames MUST
contain 1–255 UTF-8 bytes, exclude `/` and NUL, and differ from `.` and `..`. MIME types MUST be
valid and at most 255 bytes. Xattr names MUST contain 1–255 bytes without NUL, and combined xattr
key/value bytes MUST NOT exceed 32 KiB.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-attribute-shape
`Attr.size` MUST be the logical file size and MUST be zero for directories. `Attr.metadata` MUST be
present when extended metadata was requested and absent otherwise unless an RPC explicitly says
otherwise. Present metadata with an empty xattr map MUST mean metadata was fetched and no xattrs
exist; absence MUST mean metadata was not fetched.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;api] dfs-visible-parents
`Attr.parent` MUST identify the parent on the caller's canonical visible path. Virtual root MUST be
its own parent; virtual shared, visible top-level objects, and the accessible stored tenant root
MUST have virtual root as parent. Direct entry points under `/shared` MUST have virtual shared as
parent; other objects MUST use their visible parent's real ID. Hidden ancestor names and IDs MUST
NOT be exposed through `parent` or `ExtendedMetadata.full_path`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-canonical-paths
Returned extended metadata MUST include `full_path`, an absolute path in the caller's namespace with
`/` separators and no trailing slash except for `/` itself. Virtual root and the accessible stored
tenant root MUST use `/`; virtual shared MUST use `/shared`. The canonical path MUST prefer the
ordinary root, otherwise enter `/shared` through the nearest readable ancestor with a matching
explicit ALLOW, including the object itself, using its returned `basename--<object-id>` entry name.
DENY MUST NOT create entry points. Descendants MUST use ordinary basenames. `parent` MUST follow
that path even when lookup/listing used another alias. Path selection MUST use the attributes' store
snapshot and session subjects.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;performance] dfs-on-demand-paths
Full paths MUST be computed on demand, not stored on every descendant. Ancestor renames, moves, and
grant changes MUST be able to change visible paths without changing object identity or file bytes
and without requiring descendant path rewrites.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-creation-time
Returned extended metadata MUST include `created`. Every real object, including the tenant root,
MUST receive its creation timestamp at creation. It MUST be read-only and unchanged by writes,
metadata or grant changes, renames, and moves. Virtual projections MUST return zero.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-object-version-ordering
`Attr.attr_version` and `Attr.content_version` MUST be positive monotonically increasing uint64
values, with gaps allowed and no wrap or reset during the object's lifetime. Clients MUST compare
each field only against that field for the same tenant and object. Attribute versions and content
versions of all directories MUST additionally be scoped to the same session's visible namespace.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-attribute-version
`attr_version` MUST advance when attributes or extended metadata change, including size, mode,
timestamps, MIME type, xattrs, own name, and parent. It MUST reflect effective mode and caller-visible
parent/path changes from ancestors or authorization, resolved on read without requiring stored
descendant version updates. Comparisons MUST require fresh authorization; equal versions MUST NOT
grant access.
Fetching optional metadata or returning a newer `ReadView` MUST NOT itself advance the version.
Version fields MUST be excluded from attribute-change detection. Content mutations MUST advance the
attribute version when they change size or timestamps.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-file-content-version
A regular file's `content_version` MUST start at 1 and advance atomically with every nonempty write
and every file-size change, including truncation and extension. Nonempty writes of identical bytes
MUST still advance it. Mode, timestamp, MIME type, xattr, grant, rename, and move changes alone MUST
NOT advance it.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-directory-content-version
A real directory's `content_version` MUST start at 1 and advance atomically with changes to its
immediate session-visible entry-name/object-ID mapping, including creation, removal, rename, moves,
replacement, and visibility changes caused by grants. Projected visibility changes MUST be resolved
on read without requiring stored version updates on every affected directory. Changes only to a
child's attributes or contents MUST NOT advance it. Moving or renaming the directory itself MUST
advance its attribute version and affected parents' content versions, but MUST leave its own content
version unchanged when its entries are unchanged.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-projection-content-version
Virtual root/shared content versions MUST be positive and advance when their session-visible entry
mappings change, including changes from grants or topology. Ordering MUST survive servers and
restarts for the same session view. Version comparisons MUST NOT replace authorization or establish
a snapshot across listing pages.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-read-view-ordering
`ReadView.store_version` and `ReadView.auth_version` MUST each be nonnegative, tenant-wide monotonic
int64 versions that never reset or wrap. Gaps and repeated observations of the same version are
allowed; these are neither timestamps nor operation counts. Clients MUST compare like fields for the
same tenant. Monotonicity MUST describe state ordering, not response arrival order; responses and
permitted authorization replicas MAY expose older versions after newer ones.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-read-view-snapshots
For reads, `store_version` MUST identify the supplying store snapshot; for mutations it MUST
identify the successful commit, or the checked snapshot when no stored changes occur. `auth_version`
MUST identify the permission/topology state used for authorization. Each returned `Attr.view` MUST
identify that object's data and authorization snapshots. The two fields MUST NOT promise a common
snapshot, RAM-tree application of a mutation, or replace per-object attribute/content versions.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;backend] dfs-authorization-version-ordering
Authorization versions MUST use one tenant-wide ordering across instances, restarts, tree rebuilds,
and FDB fallback. The same authorization snapshot MUST retain the same version on every instance and
authorization path; equal versions MUST identify the same authorization state. Process-local or
independent RAM/fallback counters MUST NOT supply these versions.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-create-tenant
`CreateTenant` MUST create an empty real root directory and return its real ID and the new tenant
administration key. Root grants MUST be deduplicated, limited to 512 distinct values, attached to
the root, and inherited by future descendants. Existing tenant IDs MUST fail with `ALREADY_EXISTS`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-create-session
`CreateSession` MUST deduplicate at most 512 distinct subjects into a fixed subject set; subjects
MAY have no matching ALLOW attachments yet. It MUST return a session identifier distinct from its
credential, the session key, expiration, tenant ID, and real tenant root ID. Sessions MUST live in
server memory, expire after one hour, and be lost on restart. Renewal and subject-set changes MUST
require a new session rather than a renewal or update RPC.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-current-session
`CurrentSession` MUST return the authenticated session with an empty `session_key`, without
reissuing a credential or changing its subjects or expiration.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-close-session
`CloseSession` MUST return only after admitted mutations finish and the session is invalidated.
Subsequent calls with that session key MUST fail authentication.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-list-grants
`ListGrants` MUST return explicit ALLOW/DENY attachments only, excluding inherited grants, ordered
by variant (ALLOW before DENY), then ALLOW subject in UTF-8 byte order, then numeric mode. `limit`
MUST be 1–512. `after` MUST be an opaque exclusive cursor, omitted for the first page. Clients MUST
pass `next_after` unchanged as `after`; its absence MUST indicate completion.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-update-grants
`UpdateGrants` MUST atomically apply at most 512 changes with unique grant values. Repeating a value
with different removal flags MUST be invalid. Attachments not included in changes MUST remain
unchanged; detaching an ancestor grant MUST NOT remove independent descendant attachments. Permission
changes, including DENY, MUST remain subject to the authorization freshness bound and MUST NOT promise
immediate revocation.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-stat-results
`Stat` MUST accept 1–256 references and return an `AttrBatch`. Results MUST correspond to inputs by
position, including repeated references; successful results MUST identify the object in `Attr.id`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-stat-metadata
`Stat` and `Lookup` with `include_metadata=true` MUST populate each successful object's extended
metadata, including full path, from the same FDB snapshot as its attributes. False or omitted MUST
omit metadata while leaving it covered by `attr_version`. Virtual metadata MUST use
`inode/directory`, an empty xattr map, `created=0`, and `/` or `/shared` as appropriate.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-lookup
`Lookup` MUST accept 1–256 parent/name pairs and return an `AttrBatch` with exactly one result per
pair in input order. Each name MUST be an immediate child basename, not a path. A missing or
inaccessible child MUST produce a per-result `NOT_FOUND` without preventing other results. Each real
parent MUST be accessible to the caller. Results MUST obey the same attribute/error shape, per-object
read views, metadata rules, and 4 MiB response budget as `Stat`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-list-pagination
`List` MUST return immediate children with current attributes, obey a required limit of 1–4,096
entries, and fit a 4 MiB encoded response budget. `after` MUST be exclusive and omitted initially;
clients MUST pass `next_after` unchanged and continue until it is absent, including after an empty
page. Ordinary directories MUST be ordered by basename; shared MUST use object-ID cursors.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-list-refresh
Clients MUST refresh pages through `List`, without a separate listing token or version precondition.
A directory content version obtained through `Stat` and checked through `Validate` MAY renew access
to bindings cached at that version, but MUST NOT validate cached child attributes or contents. Those
MUST be checked separately or refetched. All attributes returned in an `EntryPage` MUST carry the
same `Attr.view` for that request; the page MUST NOT contain a separate view. Independent pages MUST
NOT promise one snapshot, even after validation. These rules MUST apply to real and virtual
directories alike.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-virtual-listings
Virtual root MUST expose visible top-level entries plus shared. Virtual shared MUST expose readable
entry points with a matching explicit ALLOW and names suffixed `--<object-id>`, without requiring
access to their parents. DENY MUST NOT create entry points. Entries MUST pass full root-to-object
evaluation, including descendants reopened by a deeper ALLOW below an inaccessible parent. Clients
MUST use returned real IDs for subsequent metadata, content, and mutation operations on those
objects.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-read-range
`Read` MUST return at most the requested length, limited to 1 MiB, from the zero-based byte offset.
Reads MUST stop at EOF and return empty bytes at or beyond EOF. Directories MUST fail with
`IS_DIRECTORY`. Returned bytes and attributes MUST share the same snapshot, identified by
`ReadData.object.view`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-read-precondition
An omitted `ReadRequest.content_version` MUST impose no precondition. A supplied zero MUST fail with
`INVALID_INPUT`, and a mismatched positive version MUST fail with `STALE_VIEW`. Metadata-only
changes MUST NOT fail this precondition; returned attributes MUST reflect the current read snapshot.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-read-files
`ReadFiles` MUST accept 1–256 real IDs and account for each input with either a result or an omitted
ID. Results MUST preserve relative input order. Success MUST include attributes and whole-file data,
including present empty bytes for an empty file, with no error; failure MUST contain an error
instead of attributes/data. Attributes and contents MUST share one FDB snapshot. All returned
attributes MUST carry the same `Attr.view`; the batch MUST NOT contain a separate view. Files over
1 MiB MUST receive individual `CAPACITY` errors; other files that cannot fit the 4 MiB reply MUST be
omitted without being downloaded.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-validate-input
`Validate` MUST accept 1–256 checks. Each `VersionCheck` MUST supply at least one positive attribute
or content version, or both. Neither version supplied or any supplied zero MUST reject the whole
request with `INVALID_INPUT`. Omitted versions MUST NOT be compared.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-validate-outcomes
`Validate` MUST return one result per check in input order and check authorization before comparing
versions against the same current object view. For an existing authorized object, all supplied
versions matching MUST yield `UNCHANGED`; any difference MUST yield `CHANGED`. Denied access,
absence, and other check failures MUST take precedence and yield `DENIED`, `MISSING`, or `ERROR`,
with error details. Backend failure MAY fail the entire RPC rather than establish partial freshness.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-validation-coverage
`UNCHANGED` MUST renew read access, not write access, and validate only supplied versions from the
same session view where session-scoped. Attribute checks MUST cover attributes and extended
metadata, including visible parent/path; content checks MUST cover file bytes or directory
entry-name/object-ID bindings. A check of one version MUST NOT validate the other. Even both
matching directory versions MUST NOT validate children's attributes or contents. `CHANGED` MUST NOT
identify which version differed. Clients MUST refresh relevant state through `Stat`,
`Read`/`ReadFiles`, or `List`; fresh attributes MAY establish that bytes still match without
redownloading them.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-apply-budget
`Apply.operations` MUST be nonempty, each `Operation` MUST select exactly one variant, and the
encoded request MUST fit 1 MiB. FDB transaction write budgets MAY still reject the RPC with
`CAPACITY`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency;backend] dfs-apply-transaction
`Apply` MUST execute operations in request order within one FDB transaction, including operations on
different objects. Later operations MUST see earlier successful changes. Each operation MUST finish
filesystem validation before staging writes; a validation failure MUST leave state unchanged for
that operation, record its error, and allow later operations to continue. All successful operations
MUST commit together. Storage/commit failures MUST affect the whole transaction attempt, not appear
as isolated operation errors. No result MUST be returned before commit.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-apply-results
`Apply` MUST return exactly one `OperationResult` per input in request order, containing exactly one
of `mutation` or `error`. Successful removal MUST still contain `mutation`. Returned attributes MUST
reflect final committed state; objects removed later in the batch MUST have no returned attributes.
`Mutation.related` MUST contain other returned objects affected by the operation. Unless required by
the operation, parents changed only by membership and associated version bookkeeping MAY be omitted;
clients MUST invalidate those parents' attributes and listing pages. Attribute/content versions MUST
advance atomically with their corresponding changes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;backend] dfs-apply-view
Every `Attr` returned in `Mutation.object` or `Mutation.related` across an `OperationBatch` MUST
carry the same `Attr.view`, with the batch commit version and authorization-state version used by
the committed attempt. If no stored changes occur, the store version MUST be the snapshot checked
by that attempt. A mutation returning no attributes MUST NOT carry a separate view.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:concurrency] dfs-apply-disconnection
Accepted `Apply` work MUST continue after disconnection. A lost response MUST NOT imply failure;
without an idempotency key, callers MUST NOT blindly replay operations with uncertain outcomes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-create-operation
`CreateOperation` MUST create an empty file or directory under an authorized real directory, using a
fresh caller-supplied UUIDv7. Omitted MIME type MUST default to `inode/directory` for directories or
`application/octet-stream` for files. Name or ID collisions MUST fail with `ALREADY_EXISTS`. Success
MUST return the created object's final attributes unless a later operation removes it.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-update-operation
`UpdateOperation` MUST apply a metadata patch to an authorized object, leave omitted fields
unchanged, and accept all changes as one operation or none if validation fails. Xattr changes MUST
affect individual keys, not replace the whole map; absent value MUST remove a key, while present
empty bytes MUST set an empty value. `size` MUST truncate/extend a regular file; growth MUST expose
zeroes and truncation MUST discard bytes beyond the new size. Success MUST return final attributes
if the object survives.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;concurrency] dfs-write-operation
`WriteOperation` MUST write an authorized regular file and extend it as needed with zero-filled
sparse gaps. `append=true` MUST ignore offset and choose current EOF atomically, observing earlier
successful operations in the batch; otherwise offset MUST be zero-based bytes. Data MUST fit the
overall `Apply` budget. Success MUST return final attributes if the file survives.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-rename-operation
`RenameOperation` MUST preserve object identity and require access to the source and affected
parents. Replacement MUST require `replace=true`, the same kind, and an empty destination directory
when replacing a directory. Moving a directory into itself or a descendant MUST be rejected.
Renames/parent changes MUST advance the object's attribute version and affected parents' listing
content versions; later metadata MUST reflect new full paths, including moved descendants. Success
MUST return final attributes if the object survives.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-remove-operation
`RemoveOperation` MUST require access to the object and parent, and `directory` MUST match the
object's kind. Nonempty directories MUST fail with `NOT_EMPTY`; recursive removal MUST explicitly
remove descendants first. Success MUST contain `mutation` without primary object attributes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-search-query
`Search.query` MUST contain at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes. Empty/whitespace-only queries MUST search
metadata only. Nonempty text MUST match any normalized token across selected fields with OR; empty
fields MUST select both NAME and CONTENT. Content-only selection MUST exclude directories;
directories MUST match their own name/metadata. Limit MUST be 1–100, defaulting to 20.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-search-scope
Omitted scope MUST search session-visible tenant objects. A supplied scope MUST name an authorized
real directory and exclude that directory itself; recursion MUST default to true, with false
selecting immediate children only. Virtual projections MUST NOT be indexed.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api] dfs-search-filters
Search filter fields MUST combine with AND. Name and prefix predicates MUST be exact; at most 32
MIME types MUST combine with OR, and size/mtime bounds MUST be inclusive. MIME/size predicates MUST
select files and MUST NOT combine with `kind=DIRECTORY`. At most 64 xattr predicates MUST combine
with AND; omitted values MUST test existence, and present values MUST test byte-exact equality,
including empty bytes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;security] dfs-search-freshness
Search MUST use Elasticsearch and fail with `UNAVAILABLE` if it is disabled or unavailable. Every
hit MUST be permission-checked, and deleted objects and stale indexed content/metadata MUST be
suppressed. Matching content versions MUST establish only content freshness; indexed names and
metadata MUST be checked separately. Unsupported content formats MUST remain searchable by
name/metadata. Returned parents and attribute versions MUST use the caller's namespace. Shared
indexes MUST NOT store session-specific paths; those MUST be resolved authoritatively through
`Stat(include_metadata=true)`.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;performance] dfs-search-results
Search MUST return at most limit hits and expose no public cursor, score, or total-hit count. Hit
names MUST be basenames, not canonical paths. All returned hit attributes MUST carry the same
`Attr.view` for the request; `SearchResults` MUST NOT contain a separate view. File excerpts MUST be
at most 512 characters and MUST be absent for directories. Evaluation MUST be bounded to 4,096
candidates, ten seconds of retrieval, and a 1 MiB response. `partial` MUST indicate bounded
evaluation, not indexing freshness. Backend failures MUST be errors, not successful empty results.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:api;error-handling] dfs-error-details
RPC failures MUST carry a gRPC status with protobuf `ErrorDetails { code }` in its details. Batch
calls MUST use the same details for individual failures. Error codes MUST remain stable: INTERNAL,
INVALID_INPUT, NOT_FOUND, FORBIDDEN, UNAUTHENTICATED, ALREADY_EXISTS, NOT_DIRECTORY, IS_DIRECTORY,
NOT_EMPTY, CAPACITY, UNAVAILABLE, UNSUPPORTED, NAME_TOO_LONG, and STALE_VIEW.
